htop color themes
=================

Theme files (*.theme) let you customize htop colors without recompiling.

Search order (later entries override earlier ones with the same id):
  1. $HTOP_DATADIR/themes/          (packaged themes, usually $prefix/share/htop/themes)
  2. $SYSCONFDIR/htop/themes/       (system-wide, e.g. /etc/htop/themes)
  3. $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/htop/themes/  or  ~/.config/htop/themes/
  4. $HTOP_THEME_DIR/               (developer override)

Select a theme in Setup (F2) → Colors, or set in ~/.config/htop/htoprc:

  theme_name=dracula

Or from the command line:

  htop --theme=dracula

File format
-----------

  # comments start with # or ;
  name=Display Name
  force_black_bg=0

  # ELEMENT = foreground background [attributes...]
  DEFAULT_COLOR = white default
  PROCESS_BASENAME = cyan default bold
  FUNCTION_BAR = black cyan

Colors: black red green yellow blue magenta cyan white gray default
  (purple is an alias for magenta; grey is an alias for gray)

Attributes: bold reverse dim underline normal blink

Attribute-only values are also allowed:

  BAR_BORDER = bold
  PROCESS = normal

Unknown element names are ignored so themes stay forward-compatible.
Missing elements inherit the built-in Default scheme.

The theme id used in htoprc is the filename without the .theme suffix.
